1. DEFINITIONS
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
"Work"            All files in this repository authored by the Author, in any form: source code, game rules and rulebooks, balance
                  data, lore, text, 3D models, card designs and art, documentation, tools, data, logs and design history. Contributions
                  (section 5) become part of the Work. Third-Party Components are not part of the Work.
"Game"            The Tower Game, and the earlier or related versions in this repository (including the archived "Lotus" version).
"Rules"           The written rules of the Game as stated in the Work (rulebook, manifesto, rules documents, balance tables), as distinct
                  from the code, models, art, names and wording that express them.
"Printable Materials"  The rules, the cards (including those the Provided Pages generate), and the 3D model files in the Work.
"Browser"         A general-purpose web browser (for example Firefox, Chrome, Safari or Edge) running on your own device.
"Provided Pages"  The HTML pages in this repository, and pages the Author hosts, loaded in a Browser; and pages that belong to a DLC
                  published under this license, loaded in a Browser.
"Provided Scripts" The scripts in this repository that serve the Provided Pages or exercise the Game (run.sh, tools/serve.py,
                  tools/server.mjs, tools/tg.mjs, test/sim.mjs and the like).
"DLC"             Any expansion, add-on, scenario, unit, rule set, card set, model set, map or other content made to extend, modify or
                  be used with the Game, in any medium.
"Derivative"      A modification of, or work based on, the Work, including every DLC.
"Commercial Use"  Any use aimed at, or resulting in, commercial advantage or money: selling, renting, licensing for a fee, charging for
                  access, subscriptions, advertising, sponsorship, donations or tips tied to the Work, crowd-funding, merchandising,
                  bundling with anything sold, use in a paid event, product or service, or hosting behind a paywall.
"Third-Party Components"  Material that belongs to others and carries its own license, listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
"You"             Any person who obtains a copy of the Work.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. WHAT YOU MAY DO  (free of charge, non-commercial)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
2.1  Inspect.   View, read and study every file in the Work.
2.2  Play.      Play the Game at will, for free, by loading the Provided Pages in a Browser, including served from your own machine with
     the Provided Scripts, alone or with other people. You may run the Provided Scripts to serve or examine the Game.
2.3  Print.     Print the Printable Materials and make a physical (tabletop) version of the Game: print the rules and cards, and
     fabricate the 3D models (for example with a 3D printer) — for your own use and to give away free of charge. You may have a
     third-party printing or fabrication service make items for You, provided the service uses the items only to deliver them
     to You and does not sell or distribute them.
2.4  Share.     Copy and redistribute the Work, unmodified, free of charge, provided this license and all notices stay with it.
     Cloning or forking the repository on the platform that hosts it is included.
2.5  Build.     Modify the Work and create Derivatives, including DLCs, and publish them free of charge, provided that (a) they are
     released under this same license, exactly, with no added restrictions, (b) You mark your changes and keep the credit to the
     Author and to the original, (c) You make clear that unofficial content is unofficial, and (d) section 5 applies to them.
2.6  Show.      Review, discuss, teach, stream or record the Game and write about it, including on platforms that carry advertising
     or sponsorship, so long as the Work itself is not sold or put behind a paywall and the Game is not presented as yours.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.1  No commercial use.  You may not make Commercial Use of the Work, of anything printed or made from it (printed rules or cards,
     fabricated models, physical recreations of the Game), or of any Derivative or DLC. Printed or fabricated items may be given
     away; they may not be sold, rented, auctioned, traded for value, crowd-funded, or placed in any commercial setting.
3.2  Browser only; no native builds.  The Game may be run only in a Browser, from the Provided Pages. You may not package, wrap,
     compile, convert, port, emulate or re-implement the Game or any part of the Work as, or to run inside, a native, desktop,
     mobile or console application or executable, and You may not launch the Game through any such application, launcher or wrapper.
     This applies in particular to Microsoft Windows and Apple macOS and includes installers, app bundles, executables,
     embedded-browser or webview shells (for example Electron, NW.js, Tauri, Cordova or Capacitor), game launchers and store
     listings. A Browser opening a Provided Page is permitted; a program whose purpose is to run the Game is not. (The Author may grant
     separate, written permission for specific cases.)
3.3  No added restrictions; no relicensing.  You may not apply any other license to the Work or a Derivative, nor add restrictions to this
     one, nor use technical measures to prevent others from using the Work as this license allows.
3.4  Credit and names.  You may not present the Work as your own, and You may not use the Author's name or the names "The Tower Game"
     or "Lotus" in a way that suggests endorsement of, or affiliation with, anything You make or do, or in the name of anything sold.

